From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(approval): a session clone of a pinned release is the
 operator's own variant

approvals.trusted_pins lists "<repo URL>@<ref>" entries. A session clone of that repo made with exactly that branch or tag (and no option that runs code or fetches more) is not Code from External, as a clone from approvals.trusted_sources is not. Another ref, branch, fork or look-alike host still is, and so is a clone that a later git checkout, fetch, pull or remote command moves.

Talaria's Hermes image is the pinned upstream release plus its patches, so building and testing the patched tree needs no card. There is no default.
